The United Nations Development Program (UNDP) works with governments, development partners, financial institutions, the private sector and communities to advance sustainable development and strengthen resilience. Through its work on sustainable finance, UNDP supports countries to mobilize and align public and private finance with national development priorities and the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).

The SDG Finance and Investment Portfolio strengthens Tanzania's financing ecosystem by mobilizing diversified finance to accelerate the SDGs. As a collaborative platform, it convenes government, the private sector, financial institutions, civil society and development partners to address financing gaps and enable investment. Its work spans public finance for the SDGs; investment promotion and facilitation; and insurance and risk finance. Across these areas, the Portfolio develops investment pipelines, tests financing instruments, promotes SDG-aligned investment, supports sustainable debt and public financing, and builds resilience, protects lives and advances inclusive economic growth. The Program Associate will provide portfolio coordination, administration, procurement, stakeholder engagement, monitoring, reporting, communications, event-management and knowledge-management support. Under matrix reporting, the incumbent will report directly to the National Program Coordinator for functional supervision and work under the Head of the Portfolio's strategic guidance and portfolio-level oversight.

Scope of Work

1. Support program and project planning, implementation and coordination:

- Support preparation, implementation and updating workplans, activity schedules, results frameworks, project trackers, and deliverable schedules in consultation with responsible managers;

- Coordinate day-to-day follow-up of assigned projects and workstreams; track milestones, deadlines, risks, deliverables and stakeholder commitments; and flag emerging issues for timely management action;

- Coordinate strategic and technical meetings, high-level forums and physical or virtual project team meetings; manage invitations, agendas, background materials, presentations, minutes, transcription or translation, action trackers and follow-up;

- Support consultations, workshops, training, launches, innovation challenges, investment events and forums, field activities and missions, working with internal units, partners, consultants and service providers;

- Draft or contribute to terms of reference, concept notes, project documents, implementation plans, presentations, correspondence, high-level briefs and meeting packs.

2. Provide administrative, procurement, event-management and operational support:

- Support preparation and monitoring of project budgets, procurement plans, implementation schedules and administrative trackers in accordance with applicable UNDP rules, policies and procedures:

- Support e-requisitions, procurement, contracting, consultant, vendor, travel and payment processes, including non-PO transactions, in accordance with assigned system roles and UNDP procedures;

- Coordinate event logistics and service providers for meetings, high-level forums, investment and innovation events and communication assignments, including venue, graphic-design, photography and videography services;

- Maintain consultant and contract deliverable schedules, vendor and payment-supporting documents, programme correspondence, project files and other complete, organized and auditready records.

3. Support stakeholder, partnership and thematic portfolio engagement:

- Support engagement with government institutions, regulators, United Nations entities, development partners, financial institutions, investors, businesses, innovation actors, civil society, academia, media and other stakeholders;

- Support activities across the Portfolio's thematic areas, including public finance, investment promotion and facilitation, innovation, insurance and risk finance, and related sustainable-finance initiatives;

- Prepare stakeholder briefs, partner profiles, high-level speeches, talking points, presentations, correspondence and meeting materials and maintain engagement calendars, databases and records of commitments and decisions;

- Facilitate information flow among stakeholders, consultants and UNDP teams and support followup on partnerships, joint activities, events, knowledge platforms and resource-mobilization opportunities.

4. Support project monitoring, reporting and knowledge management:

- Collect, consolidate, review and synthesize implementation and results updates from projects, consultants and partners, ensuring completeness, quality, consistency and timely submission;

- Maintain trackers for activities, outputs, indicators, deliverables, risks and agreed actions and support monitoring against approved workplans and results frameworks;

- Contribute to project, progress, donor, corporate and annual reports, management updates, presentations and newsletters that communicate results to internal and external audiences;

- Document progress, challenges, lessons learned, good practices, impact stories, stakeholder insights and recommendations and maintain supporting evidence for reported results and adaptive programming.

5. Support strategic communications, advocacy and content development:

- Contribute to project and portfolio communication strategies, advocacy campaigns and content plans aligned with program objectives, UNDP branding and partner-visibility requirements;

- Draft and edit high-level briefs, speeches, talking points, press releases, media advisories, articles, blogs, human-interest stories, fact sheets, knowledge briefs, newsletters, presentations, infographics and multimedia content;

- Coordinate content publication and dissemination across websites, social media, email, print and events; support media outreach; and ensure editorial quality, consistent messaging and partner visibility;

- Monitor digital analytics, media coverage and public engagement to improve communications and advocacy, and maintain an organized repository of content, communication assets and knowledge products;

- Perform other duties within the functional profile as deemed necessary for the efficient functioning of the Office and the Organization.

